          "markdown": "Starting a kids football team requires organizing key officials, securing a venue, and affiliating with your local governing body.\n\n### 1. Appoint Key Roles and Safeguarding\n\n- **Committee:** Assign a chairperson, secretary, and treasurer to handle admin [0.15].\n- **Welfare Officer:** Appoint a dedicated Club Welfare Officer, which is mandatory for youth football [0.14].\n- **DBS Checks:** Ensure all coaches and volunteers complete standard background checks and basic safeguarding courses [0.15].\n\n### 2. Plan Finances and Affiliation\n\n- **Budget:** Calculate costs for pitch hire, kit, balls, insurance, and league fees [0.15].\n- **Funding:** Collect player subscriptions or look into local community grants.\n- **Affiliation:** Register your team through official channels like the [The FA](https://www.thefa.com/-/media/cfa/surreyfa/files/clubs/setting-up-a-club.ashx?la=en) or your local County Football Association [0.13]. You can manage this process via the [FA Clubs Portal](https://avecsport.com/blog/complete-guide-to-starting-a-kids-football-club) [0.15].\n\n### 3. Secure Facilities and Equipment\n\n- **Pitches:** Book a local council or private grass pitch for matches and training [0.13].\n- **Gear:** Purchase goals, cones, bibs, match balls, and a first-aid kit [0.13].\n- **Insurance:** Secure compulsory Public Liability and Personal Accident insurance [0.13, 0.14].\n\n### 4. Recruit Players and Coaches\n\n- **Spread the Word:** Advertise via local schools, community groups, and social media [0.15].\n- **Coaches:** Bring in volunteers to run sessions [0.15], encouraging them to earn formal qualifications over time [0.15].\n- **Registration:** Host a taster session to register players and welcome parents [0.15].\n\nIf you'd like, let me know:\n\n- What **age group** you plan to coach\n- Whether you want to join a **competitive league** or just run **training sessions** \n\nI can give you more targeted advice on rules and pitch sizes.",
